    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d401-a1">

                <pb facs="0628" n="532" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg532"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 1.—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Arbizu to Mr. Biddle.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Relations of Salvador</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1872-05-03"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi>
                            3, 1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: By the decree which I have the
                    honor to transmit by the present opportunity you will see that the government of
                    Salvador, consulting its interests, has found itself under the necessity of
                    accepting the state of war which the government of Honduras, presided over by
                    General Don Jose Ma. Medina, has provoked.</p>
                <p>The reasons of this government for that resolve are comprised in the
                    considerations” of said decree, a determination which has been forced by the
                    most imperious necessity, to which it has been indispensable to sacrifice
                    momentarily the peace of these countries.</p>
                <p>In this connection, I have the honor to repeat myself, with every consideration,
                    your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GREGORIO ARBIZU.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
